crypto.subtle against a browser
===============================

These pages check vita/js/subtle.js and vita/js/subtle.c against a real
browser, run natively in the test harness (deps/netsurf/nsmonkey) and in
Chromium. They add to the web platform tests in tests/wpt/WebCryptoAPI,
which scripts/wpt-run.sh runs.

kat.html
    Every deterministic operation on fixed inputs -- digests, HMAC,
    PBKDF2, HKDF, AES-GCM/CBC/CTR/KW, ECDH, Ed25519, X25519, key export --
    and the error each bad call gives, printed as "OUT <name> <hex or
    error>". Run it in both and diff the sorted OUT lines; they should
    not differ.

gen.html, check.html, join.py
    What has random parts -- key generation, ECDSA and RSA signatures,
    RSA-OAEP -- is checked across the two: gen.html makes keys, signs and
    encrypts in one browser, and check.html imports every key in every
    format, verifies, decrypts and agrees ECDH and X25519 secrets in the
    other.
    gen.html prints its result in numbered "RES" pieces, because the
    harness cuts long console lines; join.py puts them back together:

      nsmonkey ... gen.html | grep 'console: RES ' | python3 join.py > vec.js

    then load check.html in the other browser (served over HTTP for
    Chromium, as a file for the harness). Do it in both directions.
    vec.js is generated and not kept.
